course: dictionary
lesson: 5635
title: Linen: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Linen is a strong, cool cloth made from the flax plant. Read this: «Egyptians wrapped the body in linen and placed it in a decorated coffin.» The sentence shows that linen is cloth you can wrap things in.
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Linen can also mean sheets, pillowcases, tablecloths and towels, even when they are made of cotton. In the list «the boathouse, the fish-pond, the walled kitchen-garden, the pig-styes, the stables, the dairy, the linen-presses», linen is not the plant. The rooms in the list are all parts of a big house, so linen-presses must be places that hold household cloths.
explain: Context clues tell you which meaning you need. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Linen is a strong, cool cloth made from the flax plant.
fact: Linen can also mean sheets, pillowcases, tablecloths and towels, even when they are made of cotton.
fact: In church, the white cloths used on the altar for communion are called altar linens.
fact: The ancient Egyptians wrapped mummies in linen.
fact: Flax fibres are spun into linen thread.
exercise: «Bodies were dried with a special salt and wrapped in linen to make mummies.» What was the linen used for in this sentence? | A wooden coffin | *Cloth to wrap the bodies | A special salt | A kind of film
exercise: Mia's gran says, «Put fresh linen on the beds.» What does linen mean here? | Cotton socks only | A type of kitchen garden | Flax plants growing in a field | *Sheets and pillowcases
exercise: «Flax fibres are spun into linen thread.» What is linen made from? | *Flax | Cotton only | Salt | Wood
test: «He tells her about the boathouse, the fish-pond, the walled kitchen-garden and the linen-presses.» In this list, what are linen-presses most likely to be? | Dairies for making butter | *Cupboards or rooms for storing household linen | Stables for horses | Ponds where fish live
test: Priya says, «The altar linens were freshly washed.» What are altar linens? | Plants growing beside the church | Sheets for a bed | Warm coats for winter | *White cloths used on the altar in church
exam: Which sentence uses linen to mean the cloth itself, not household sheets? | The linen cupboard is full | Put fresh linen on the beds | *Linen is a strong, cool cloth made from the flax plant | The linen-presses are upstairs
